---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/+$/, '');
---

<Layout title="Methodology & Model Card · gh-breakout">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-header">
      <div>
        <h1>Methodology & Model Card</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
          Mathematical formulation, candidate constraints, rolling-origin evaluation, and known limitations.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="badge badge-accent">Champion: 20261019-b5ff585</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Overview Grid -->
    <div class="grid-2" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Candidate Definition</h2>
        <p>The candidate universe is computed with the exact same SQL for historical training and daily live scoring:</p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
          <li><strong>Age:</strong> Repository age ≤ 90 days since first observed activity in GH Archive.</li>
          <li><strong>Star volume:</strong> Total cumulative stars observed before snapshot date <em>D</em> &lt; 200.</li>
          <li><strong>Recent momentum:</strong> At least 5 stars gained in the 14-day window <code>[D-14, D)</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>Exclusions:</strong> No forks (<code>is_fork = false</code>), mirrors, or bot-owned repositories.</li>
          <li><strong>Point-in-time correctness:</strong> Snapshot <em>D</em> represents the world as known at 00:00:00 UTC. Features read strictly <code>created_at &lt; D</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Label Definition</h2>
        <p>What constitutes a breakout?</p>
        <ul style="margin-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
          <li><strong>Primary Label (<code>breakout_rel</code>):</strong> A candidate repo is positive if its forward 30-day star gain in <code>[D, D+30)</code> meets or exceeds the 99.5th percentile (top 0.5%) among all candidates on the same snapshot <em>D</em>, subject to a minimum floor of 100 stars.</li>
          <li><strong>Secondary Label (<code>breakout_abs</code>):</strong> Gaining at least 500 stars in the forward 30-day window.</li>
          <li><strong>Maturity:</strong> A snapshot's labels are matured only when <code>D + 30 days &le; latest fully ingested date + 1</code>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Evaluation Results & Benchmark -->
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2>Rolling-Origin Cross-Validation & Benchmark</h2>
      <p>
        Evaluated across 29 rolling folds from 2018 to 2025 with an expanding training window and a strict 30-day horizon embargo. Random train/test splits are strictly forbidden.
        Every model candidate is pitted against <strong>Baseline 1 (B1)</strong>, which ranks candidates by their 7-day star velocity.
      </p>

      <div class="table-wrapper">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Model Variant</th>
              <th>Pooled PR-AUC [95% CI]</th>
              <th>ROC-AUC</th>
              <th>Precision @ 25 [95% CI]</th>
              <th>Status</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>gh-breakout Champion (LightGBM)</strong></td>
              <td class="num"><strong>0.1081</strong> [0.1016, 0.1142]</td>
              <td class="num"><strong>0.883</strong></td>
              <td class="num"><strong>0.241</strong> [0.228, 0.255]</td>
              <td><span class="badge badge-success">Champion Promoted</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Baseline 1 (7-day star velocity)</td>
              <td class="num">0.0286 [0.0246, 0.0345]</td>
              <td class="num">0.816</td>
              <td class="num">0.109 [0.100, 0.118]</td>
              <td><span class="badge badge-neutral">Heuristic Baseline</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Baseline 2 (14-day star velocity)</td>
              <td class="num">0.0197</td>
              <td class="num">0.782</td>
              <td class="num">0.098</td>
              <td><span class="badge badge-neutral">Heuristic Baseline</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Baseline 3 (Star acceleration)</td>
              <td class="num">0.0227</td>
              <td class="num">0.795</td>
              <td class="num">0.105</td>
              <td><span class="badge badge-neutral">Heuristic Baseline</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <div>
          <h3>Precision-Recall Curve (CV)</h3>
          <img src={`${base}/figures/cv_pr_curve.png`} alt="Precision-Recall Curve" class="figure-img" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Precision @ 25 by Year</h3>
          <img src={`${base}/figures/cv_precision_by_year.png`} alt="Precision @ 25 by Year" class="figure-img" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Calibration & Reliability -->
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2>Probability Calibration & Reliability</h2>
      <p>
        Raw boosting margins are transformed via isotonic regression fit exclusively on out-of-training validation windows.
        The holdout expected calibration error (ECE) is 0.00088 and Brier score is 0.00461.
      </p>
      <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        <div>
          <img src={`${base}/figures/cv_reliability.png`} alt="Calibration Reliability Diagram" class="figure-img" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Why Calibration Matters</h3>
          <p>
            Because the base rate of true breakout repositories is only ~0.5% (1 in 200), uncalibrated models output scores that look like probabilities but cannot be interpreted as odds.
            Our calibrated probabilities reflect true empirical frequencies: if 100 repositories are assigned ~20% probability, ~20 of them will break out.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Feature Importance & SHAP -->
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
      <h2>Global Feature Importance (TreeSHAP)</h2>
      <p>
        Features span 68 live-available variables across star dynamics, contributor activity, account age distributions, tastemaker networks, and external Hacker News signals.
      </p>
      <div class="grid-2" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <div>
          <h3>Top Feature Importance</h3>
          <img src={`${base}/figures/shap_importance.png`} alt="SHAP Feature Importance" class="figure-img" />
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>SHAP Beeswarm Distribution</h3>
          <img src={`${base}/figures/shap_beeswarm.png`} alt="SHAP Beeswarm Plot" class="figure-img" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Known Limitations -->
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Known Limitations & Data Integrity Audits</h2>
      <ul style="margin-left: 1.5rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
        <li><strong>External Virality:</strong> Attention outside GitHub and Hacker News (e.g. X/Twitter, Reddit, YouTube, TikTok) is invisible to the model until star events begin arriving.</li>
        <li><strong>Events API Payload Trimming (2025-10-07):</strong> GitHub removed PR authors, commit lists, and merge flags from public events. The live champion uses only features verified to survive this trim.</li>
        <li><strong>GH Archive Star Capture Collapse (May 2025):</strong> From 2025-05-24 onward, star events in GH Archive experienced an upstream capture drop. In response, historical training is strictly capped to the trusted era (ending 2025-05-23).</li>
        <li><strong>Star Manipulation (Bots):</strong> Automated star farms are not yet filtered out in Phase 10. Phase 11 introduces our dedicated fake-star detector and network anomaly scoring.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .figure-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }
</style>
